6. Reserved rights, settlement, and termination

6.1 All rights not expressly granted are reserved. This License grants no
rights in Tilion Inc.'s trademarks and implies no endorsement. Accurate
attribution and the notices required by this License are permitted.

6.2 Production use outside Section 3 is unauthorized from the outset,
whether or not Tilion Inc. gives notice. Tilion Inc. makes a standing offer
to settle such use at the monthly list price in force in each month of
unauthorized production use, plus 25%, counting only months after the last
applicable Grace Period ended and not covered by a subscription, and limited
to the 24 months before Tilion Inc.'s first written notice unless the
Organization made a knowingly false statement to Tilion Inc. about its
eligibility. The offer may be accepted within 30 days of that notice.
Creating an Order for the settlement within that period constitutes
acceptance while the Order is pending. Use so settled is permitted under
Section 3.2(e). Otherwise Tilion Inc.'s remedies under copyright law are
unaffected.

6.3 If you materially breach this License, Tilion Inc. may give written
notice describing the breach. If the breach is not cured, or the use is not
settled under Section 6.2, within 30 days of that notice, Tilion Inc. may
terminate your rights under this License by further written notice. No cure
period is owed for a knowingly false statement to Tilion Inc. A lapse that
is ended by restoring the subscription, by paying the Lapse Grace Period
charge, or by settlement under Section 6.2 is not a material breach.

6.4 On termination, you must stop exercising the terminated rights unless
Tilion Inc. reinstates them in writing. Termination does not affect
independently held BSD or third-party rights, the rights of recipients who
comply with this License, or any obligation or claim arising before
termination. Sections 5, 6.1, 6.4, 7, and 8 survive termination.

